commit 355d0f141fefca33fe4658589dadfc9091015276
Author: konard <drakonard@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 17:31:57 2026 +0000

    fix: no closing references for closed, later-created, other-PR or 'Part of' umbrella issues (#3174, #3282)
    
    The post-session link repair always required the primary issue and every
    unmentioned same-repository sub-issue, so an umbrella PR that said
    'Part of #N' got 'Fixes' lines for the umbrella and its whole subtree.
    The repair now defers sub-issues that are already closed, were created
    after the PR was opened, or are closed by another open pull request
    (including PRs stacked on a feature branch), and the primary issue when
    the description explicitly says the work is partial. Repository-mode
    listed issues and issues the description closes stay required. The
    pre-merge guard now also refuses merges whose GitHub links would close
    issues the pull request keeps open.

